rl":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/devsensei404/placement-portal/commit/be369767938804a1cf043802a7eacfa0b01c128b","node_id":"C_kwDOSfvAjdoAKGJlMzY5NzY3OTM4ODA0YTFjZjA0MzgwMmE3ZWFjZmEwYjAxYzEyOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/devsensei404/placement-portal/commit/9b016a6234f316c65bc0b151cb08628a8db8f161","sha":"9b016a6234f316c65bc0b151cb08628a8db8f161","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devsensei404/placement-portal/commits/9b016a6234f316c65bc0b151cb08628a8db8f161"}],"sha":"be369767938804a1cf043802a7eacfa0b01c128b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devsensei404/placement-portal/commits/be369767938804a1cf043802a7eacfa0b01c128b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/251255940?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/devsensei404","id":251255940,"login":"devsensei404","node_id":"U_kgDODvnchA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devsensei404","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devsensei404/placement-portal/commits/abe4aa7a666e8d4dfff713a59457ca6ecaebd8b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T09:09:06Z","email":"subhadeeppaul51@gmail.com","name":"devsensei404"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T09:09:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request from devsensei404/v2-overhaul-backend\n\nV2 overhaul backend ---\n\n## V3: Company / Admin / Association Architecture\n\nReplaces the flat two-role system (`APPLICANT`, `EMPLOYER`) with a full company-centric model: recruiters now belong to verified companies through a request/approval workflow, and an admin role gets moderation powers over the whole platform.\n\n### What''s new\n\n**Account types** — `AccountType` extends from `{APPLICANT, EMPLOYER}` to `{APPLICANT, EMPLOYER, COMPANY, ADMIN}`. Admin registration is gated behind a shared secret key (`admin.secret.key`), never open to public signup.\n\n**Companies** — a new `Company` entity with its own approval lifecycle (`PENDING → APPROVED / REJECTED / SUSPENDED`). Companies self-register, then wait on admin approval before becoming visible to recruiters or able to have jobs posted under them.\n\n**Recruiter–company association** — recruiters (`EMPLOYER` accounts) start `UNASSOCIATED` and request to join a verified company. Companies approve or reject these requests. Once `ACTIVE`, a recruiter can post jobs; the system enforces this server-side, not just in the UI. Recruiters can voluntarily leave a company (auto-closes their open jobs) or be unlisted by their company/admin (existing jobs/applicants stay intact, only new activity is blocked).\n\n**Jobs** — `Job.company` (free-text string) replaced with `Job.companyId` (FK). `postJob`/`updateJob` now validate the recruiter''s `listingStatus == ACTIVE` and derive `companyId` server-side — never trusting a client-submitted value. `JobDTO` gained a derived `companyName` field (batched lookup, no N+1) so job listings display and search correctly again post-migration.\n\n**Admin moderation** — company approve/reject/suspend, user ban/unban, full account deletion, recruiter unlist/relist, job/review deletion. Every admin action writes an entry to a new `AdminAuditLog`.\n\n### Security\n\nA dedicated security review was run against this branch before merge. Two blocking findings were identified and fixed:\n- **Ban enforcement was non-functional** — `User.enabled` existed at the data layer but nothing checked it during authentication or on subsequent requests. Fixed via `CustomUserDetails.isEnabled()` (blocks login) plus a per-request backstop in `SecurityUtils` (catches already-issued tokens for users banned mid-session).\n- **Unhandled exceptions leaked raw internal messages** to API clients (SQL/Hibernate details, stack info) via the global exception handler. Now logged server-side, generic message returned to the client.\n\nRemaining non-blocking findings (transactional gaps, a few consistency issues between `updateJob`/`deleteJob` guards) are tracked separately, not addressed in this PR.\n\n### Known tradeoffs\n\n- No DB migration script for the `Job.company` → `Job.companyId` change — pre-existing job rows have `companyId = null`. Accepted tradeoff for a dev-stage project, called out explicitly rather than silently.\n- No guard against an admin targeting another admin (or themselves) in account deletion — low-priority given the current trusted-operator scale of this project.\n\n### Testing\n\nVerified compiling and booting on real infrastructure. Full manual pass via `.http` requests covering: company registration → admin approval → association request/approve → job posting guard (both directions), admin ban/unban including mid-session token invalidation, admin key mismatch rejection, and the exception-leakage fix. Existing frontend confirmed working against the new backend after the `companyName` fix.\n\n### Not in this PR\n\nFrontend UI for company registration/profile, admin dashboard, and the association request flow — none of it has UI yet. Tracked as follow-up work.","tree":{"sha":"05cb567fdb281147834fe546c48d04b192fe1883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devsensei404/placement-portal/git/trees/05cb567fdb281147834fe546c48d04b192fe1883"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devsensei404/placement-portal/git/commits/abe4aa7a666e8d4dfff713a59457ca6ecaebd8b9","verification":{"payload":"tree 05cb567fdb281147834fe546c48d04b192fe1883\nparent 9b016a6234f316c65bc0b151cb08628a8db8f161\nparent d41cbed999cc4ec1133b354e0fb796ede12ed285\nauthor devsensei404 <subhadeeppaul51@gmail.com> 1785920946 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785920946 +0530\n\nMerge pull request from devsensei404/v2-overhaul-backend\n\nV2 overhaul backend ---\n\n## V3: Company / Admin / Association Architecture\n\nReplaces the flat two-role system (`APPLICANT`, `EMPLOYER`) with a full company-centric model: recruiters now belong to verified companies through a request/approval workflow, and an admin role gets moderation powers over the whole platform.\n\n### What''s new\n\n**Account types** — `AccountType` extends from `{APPLICANT, EMPLOYER}` to `{APPLICANT, EMPLOYER, COMPANY, ADMIN}`. Admin registration is gated behind a shared secret key (`admin.secret.key`), never open to public signup.\n\n**Companies** — a new `Company` entity with its own approval lifecycle (`PENDING → APPROVED / REJECTED / SUSPENDED`). Companies self-register, then wait on admin approval before becoming visible to recruiters or able to have jobs posted under them.\n\n**Recruiter–company association** — recruiters (`EMPLOYER` accounts) start `UNASSOCIATED` and request to join a verified company. Companies approve or reject these requests. Once `ACTIVE`, a recruiter can post jobs; the system enforces this server-side, not just in the UI. Recruiters can voluntarily leave a company (auto-closes their open jobs) or be unlisted by their company/admin (existing jobs/applicants stay intact, only new activity is blocked).\n\n**Jobs** — `Job.company` (free-text string) replaced with `Job.companyId` (FK). `postJob`/`updateJob` now validate the recruiter''s `listingStatus == ACTIVE` and derive `companyId` server-side — never trusting a client-submitted value. `JobDTO` gained a derived `companyName` field (batched lookup, no N+1) so job listings display and search correctly again post-migration.\n\n**Admin moderation** — company approve/reject/suspend, user ban/unban, full account deletion, recruiter unlist/relist, job/review deletion. Every admin action writes an entry to a new `AdminAuditLog`.\n\n### Security\n\nA dedicated security review was run against this branch before merge. Two blocking findings were identified and fixed:\n- **Ban enforcement was non-functional** — `User.enabled` existed at the data layer but nothing checked it during authentication or on subsequent requests. Fixed via `CustomUserDetails.isEnabled()` (blocks login) plus a per-request backstop in `SecurityUtils` (catches already-issued tokens for users banned mid-session).\n- **Unhandled exceptions leaked raw internal messages** to API clients (SQL/Hibernate details, stack info) via the global exception handler. Now logged server-side, generic message returned to the client.\n\nRemaining non-blocking findings (transactional gaps, a few consistency issues between `updateJob`/`deleteJob` guards) are tracked separately, not addressed in this PR.\n\n### Known tradeoffs\n\n- No DB migration script for the `Job.company` → `Job.companyId` change — pre-existing job rows have `companyId = null`. Accepted tradeoff for a dev-stage project, called out explicitly rather than silently.\n- No guard against an admin targeting another admin (or themselves) in account deletion — low-priority given the current trusted-operator scale of this project.\n\n### Testing\n\nVerified compiling and booting on real infrastructure. Full manual pass via `.http` requests covering: company registration → admin approval → association request/approve → job posting guard (both directions), admin ban/unban including mid-session token invalidation, admin key mismatch rejection, and the exception-leakage fix. Existing frontend confirmed working against the new backend after the `companyName` fix.\n\n### Not in this PR\n\nFrontend UI for company registration/profile, admin dashboard, and the association request flow — none of it has UI yet. Tracked as follow-up work.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcv2yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0G8QAE5zAk9q64lItIvmnSp4Gb/W\nFMCpTbLJk9jmv+rw7q7jTYwimoEdPkzuw9Fz+6jkYbwiKTK7PUiRL1QyL947Walp\nqOUM8cmsGvfYOlEIRBnIT7nLbxlPax5ZDHKpdb6BQhhgGSCAy39xhdF04GfoqWSc\nRQuV6W4sBwO1ny3qrT36mwCw8obNPZ9wjkg/Fmv33rYKYw+AZkeRGKwUg+dBpBDK\n2dXpbyccHZOLyoGxtcyDq2ArX6VlxZs/8xj1d10+G/W709/I0A2Oq6Jk3yRnlmpu\nBsbNrxDPmgriiVZC2RrG28UxSy9qbd7+w5C+UYI5sNPu1CwqNNAZQhXWtCtiASer\nffessqJOvh2sNNHTeImf1nXu1UrL1ajEIxIxlWTfJVbpO0XfiUA2HV2AEaWJoh0q\nK2Zuxf5/X9DTIzuNKByWCyuuzGVQXkJao9XeRkpYdcLn1PYBw1OSD4RdIB8ULU5h\ngQGHBBnbeMxu9oOPZ4sMJZp+D21cUnjICT/CwvQGIXqRBb6GIiuNB1o5h6mVCnuj\n8QMD6UbwFF2z31DOm6pDFGFMzneV7wdoe9st5sIIkJvnB6e7ohTq7O3rLoAwmRl4\nbZXCu3B1rr/3+3EzKOY4oMvj/hs/LAWd21YjKWxqZ/j4rJi+eDJ/QWWThz4pWNhY\nE/DwY5P5wrVQXuU391Pg\n=YbK3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-05T09:09:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/we