","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commit/7a20247be016eda07437c2bc97997c977061b2f4","node_id":"C_kwDOSf0K4doAKDdhMjAyNDdiZTAxNmVkYTA3NDM3YzJiYzk3OTk3Yzk3NzA2MWIyZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commit/1c9f4918e28c894a35194da3597e18cef0950ce4","sha":"1c9f4918e28c894a35194da3597e18cef0950ce4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commits/1c9f4918e28c894a35194da3597e18cef0950ce4"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commit/f49c4e372d25808a83bbc7bb5b75f1055e6bfb30","sha":"f49c4e372d25808a83bbc7bb5b75f1055e6bfb30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commits/f49c4e372d25808a83bbc7bb5b75f1055e6bfb30"}],"sha":"7a20247be016eda07437c2bc97997c977061b2f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commits/7a20247be016eda07437c2bc97997c977061b2f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181067701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rcs-morales","id":181067701,"login":"rcs-morales","node_id":"U_kgDOCsrftQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commits/b6009032c0f40a701d1d794108adc02fb3d22926/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T00:53:38Z","email":"ra.csmorales@gmail.com","name":"unknown"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T00:53:38Z","email":"ra.csmorales@gmail.com","name":"unknown"},"message":"fix: unify in-session vs Results grading-feedback card styling\n\nThe AI grading breakdown (correction diff, category tag, explanation)\nwas the last piece still carrying the pre-Kaiwa-Quest look: serif JP\nfont and italics on the diff strip, a hover-lift card with hard-coded\nold-teal rgba(13,115,119,…) shadows, and a \"capitalize\" mono tag with a\nmismatched 4px radius — all coming from a \"Rich AI Feedback Styling\n(Unique Custom Aesthetic)\" block. A second, later block in the same\nfile redefined every one of those same selectors again (with yet a\ndifferent look), so which properties actually rendered depended on\nwhich of the two blocks happened to declare them last.\n\nConsolidated both into one definition in style.css, used identically by\nthe in-session result badge (ui.js showResult) and the Results screen\nbreakdown list:\n- system rounded font throughout, no italics\n- flat card: --surface bg, 2px --card-border, no gradients/hover-lift\n- category tag: mono, uppercase, pill-shaped (999px), matching the\n  --tag-*-bg/--tag-*-text tokens already used for the ✓/✗ tags right\n  next to it in the Results list\n- no hard-coded legacy-teal colors — every color is a theme token, so\n  dark mode is correct too\n- dropped ~90 lines of dead/duplicate CSS (.rich-corrected-box,\n  .rich-feedback-subheader were unreferenced; the whole second\n  .rich-breakdown-* block was fully shadowed by the first)\n\nVerified in headless Edge: rendered the same sample grading result\nthrough both ui.js''s DOM-building path and Results.svelte''s markup side\nby side, in light and dark — computed card background, border, radius,\nfont, and font-style now match exactly between the two contexts (16/16\nchecks). Full unit suite passes (169).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"82067dc64bf0635d651def7558ef2c0686b21138","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/git/trees/82067dc64bf0635d651def7558ef2c0686b21138"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/git/commits/b6009032c0f40a701d1d794108adc02fb3d22926","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181067701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rcs-morales","id":181067701,"login":"rcs-morales","node_id":"U_kgDOCsrftQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commit/b6009032c0f40a701d1d794108adc02fb3d22926","node_id":"C_kwDOSf0K4doAKGI2MDA5MDMyYzBmNDBhNzAxZDFkNzk0MTA4YWRjMDJmYjNkMjI5MjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commit/1c9f4918e28c894a35194da3597e18cef0950ce4","sha":"1c9f4918e28c894a35194da3597e18cef0950ce4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commits/1c9f4918e28c894a35194da3597e18cef0950ce4"}],"sha":"b6009032c0f40a701d1d794108adc02fb3d22926","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commits/b6009032c0f40a701d1d794108adc02fb3d22926"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181067701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rcs-morales","id":181067701,"login":"rcs-morales","node_id":"U_kgDOCsrftQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commits/f49c4e372d25808a83bbc7bb5b75f1055e6bfb30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T00:19:32Z","email":"ra.csmorales@gmail.com","name":"unknown"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T00:19:32Z","email":"ra.csmorales@gmail.com","name":"unknown"},"message":"fix: stop Voicevox 429 retry spam — shared cooldown, strike-out, hidden-tab pause\n\nA rate-limited api.tts.quest turned the background warmup into an error\nstorm: every phrase got two attempts with only a 5s pause, each logging a\nfull console.error, and the loop kept grinding while the tab was\nbackgrounded — exactly when users saw the console fill up.\n\n- Any 429 (warmup, voice-pack download, status poll, or live playback)\n  now arms a shared 60s cooldown; the batch loops wait it out instead of\n  hammering the API item by item.\n- After 3 cooldown cycles without progress the batch stops entirely; the\n  next warmup trigger (deck import, session start, mode change) starts\n  it fresh.\n- The batch pauses while document.hidden — no background-tab downloads\n  burning the shared quota with nobody watching.\n- The audio-ready status poll now also detects 429 and times out after\n  30s instead of polling forever and pinning the in-flight slot.\n- 429 failures log one concise warning instead of a stacked\n  console.error per phrase; live playback behavior is unchanged.\n\nCovered by tests/ttsRateLimit.test.js (cooldown arming/expiry, strike-out\nat exactly 3 attempts over 3 minutes, hidden-tab pause/resume, mid-cooldown\ncancellation); full suite passes (160).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c3e41e89a36602afef4ae2e7281ed4aa277c62bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/git/trees/c3e41e89a36602afef4ae2e7281ed4aa277c62bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/git/commits/f49c4e372d25808a83bbc7bb5b75f1055e6bfb30","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181067701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/gists{/gis