ed_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commits/e6cab65d2c647be3720310f56399bc1d7c3e9ed3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T06:27:59Z","email":"ra.csmorales@gmail.com","name":"unknown"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T06:27:59Z","email":"ra.csmorales@gmail.com","name":"unknown"},"message":"feat: multi-deck support with local-first sync (Phase 5d step 5)\n\nIntroduce a multi-deck model on top of the previous single-QA setup:\n\n- decks.svelte.js owns a reactive deck list + active-deck pointer, migrates\n  the legacy single-deck QA_DATA on first load, and synthesizes a built-in\n  \"Sample deck\" (id: null, never persisted/deletable).\n- Decks.svelte renders the deck list with per-deck best scores and switching.\n- Imports become decks: import.js adds each parsed file as a new active deck.\n- sync.js dual-writes/pulls each deck as its own row and merges local+remote,\n  handing the merged list back via the deck-list-synced event; adds a\n  migration to allow deleting session results.\n- session/history track deckId so scores are scoped per deck; startup warms\n  the Voicevox cache via startVoicevoxWarmup.\n- Dashboard recent-list keyed by index (fixes a duplicate-timestamp crash).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"560bd759dc777b83b32e657b0f46002e2314c8ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/git/trees/560bd759dc777b83b32e657b0f46002e2314c8ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/git/commits/e6cab65d2c647be3720310f56399bc1d