:"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/commits/edafe13cb4beaa8ee6824e8dc59693c27522386f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T06:21:54Z","email":"ra.csmorales@gmail.com","name":"unknown"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T06:21:54Z","email":"ra.csmorales@gmail.com","name":"unknown"},"message":"fix: render AI furigana as ruby + surface local tense errors; add sample kanji deck\n\n- toFuriganaHtml converts Kanji{reading} markers into <ruby> tags and no longer\n  suppresses furigana when a romaji reading hint is present, so the \"Speak in\n  Japanese\" tool actually renders furigana. The translation prompt mandates\n  these markers, so plain-text output was dropping intended readings.\n- gradeWithAI adds an explicit Tense breakdown item when the local tense safety\n  net detects a past/non-past mismatch the AI missed, so the learner sees why\n  the answer was marked wrong.\n- Add sample-decks/kanji-conversation-n5-n4.json: 12 kanji-rich conversational\n  Q&A pairs for import testing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3dba3579e64518f0a2600a778deb8835c4edef8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/git/trees/3dba3579e64518f0a2600a778deb8835c4edef8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rcs-morales/tarakaiwa-web/git/commits/edafe13cb4beaa8ee6824e8dc59693c27522386f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181067701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcs-morales/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"htt