dc67fd7a4eaab6a429c867"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/viuteam/emporix-sdk/commits/46f6caa6206d975a97a1aa829f93b6159bf8df2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:26:16Z","email":"dominic.fritschi@viu.ch","name":"Dominic Fritschi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:26:16Z","email":"dominic.fritschi@viu.ch","name":"Dominic Fritschi"},"message":"fix(media): send asset updates the way the media spec takes them\n\nThe spec takes a JSON PUT only for a LINK asset (type, access and url\nrequired) and a multipart PUT for a BLOB (file and body required), and answers\n204. attachToProduct and detachFromProduct sent a JSON PUT of { type, refIds },\nwhich it rejects for either type; they now send a JSON Patch on refIds alone.\nupdate() and replaceFile() resolve to void, as they did at runtime, and the\nJSON body of update() is AssetUpdateLinkInput. The tests mocked a 200 with an\nasset for every PUT, which is what hid all three.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a752e0eb9e83be86c8f20ff4009072ba3eaa7588","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/viuteam/emporix-sdk/git/trees/a752e0eb9e83be86c8f20ff4009072ba3eaa7588"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/viuteam/emporix-sdk/git/commits/46f6caa6206d975a97a1aa829f93b6159bf8df2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/viuteam/emporix-sdk/commit/46f6caa6206d975a97a1aa829f93b6159bf8df2f","node_id":"C_kwDOSgK4RtoAKDQ2ZjZjYWE2MjA2ZDk3NWE5N2ExYWE4MjlmOTNiNjE1OWJmOGRmMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/viuteam/emporix-sdk/commit/bc8399ea591448daa728fe904d8051c1942fabdc","sha":"bc8399ea591448daa728fe904d8051c1942fabdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/viuteam/emporix-sdk/commits/bc8399ea591448daa728fe904d8051c1942fabdc"}],"sha":"46f6caa6206d975a97a1aa829f93b6159bf8df2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/viuteam/empo