pos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithun9421/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithun9421/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithun9421/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithun9421","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mithun9421/react-rendering-lab/commits/6d5a0158027e597f4c2a026ef229c75b8445774f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-20T04:24:31Z","email":"mithunmuralee94@gmail.com","name":"Mithun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-20T04:24:31Z","email":"mithunmuralee94@gmail.com","name":"Mithun"},"message":"feat: ArchitectNotes batch 4 — M22-M25\n\nObservability, memory leaks, security, incident simulator.\n\n- M22: three-signals model (metrics/logs/traces), INP measurement\n       strategy, sourcemap hosting trade-off, distributed tracing bridge,\n       RUM vs synthetic\n- M23: 3-snapshot heap technique, detached-DOM retainer chains,\n       StrictMode''s role in catching leaks, WeakRef use cases,\n       debugging prod leaks via RUM\n- M24: where React''s escape stops, strict-CSP header anatomy, token\n       storage model (memory access + http-only refresh), hydration\n       JSON injection, supply chain layers\n- M25: incident playbook minute-by-minute, FPS-vs-renders triage signal,\n       no-deploy mitigations, post-fix verification three layers,\n       blameless postmortems\n\nBuild clean. 22 of 47 lessons now have ArchitectNotes.","tree":{"sha":"c46338f5f712668b746fe913f909df8a9527c065","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mithun9421/react-rendering-lab/git/trees/c46338f5f712668b746fe913f909df8a9527c065"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mithun9421/react-rendering-lab/git/commits/6d5a0158027e597f4c2a026ef229c75b8445774f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co