"email":"metril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jagannath Pranatharthikaran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-21T04:37:26Z","email":"metril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jagannath Pranatharthikaran"},"message":"Add live preview, mosaic cameras, and two-way audio (v1.1.0)\n\nBundle a go2rtc streaming server (managed subprocess, reverse-proxied at\n/go2rtc/* under OIDC auth) and build three features on top of it:\n\n- Live preview: real-time video tiles for every camera type in the web UI\n  via the go2rtc video-rtc player (WebRTC with MSE/HLS/MJPEG fallback),\n  toggled per the camera grid. Snapshot endpoint generalized to go2rtc\n  frames for non-Frigate cameras.\n- Mosaic camera type: tile N RTSP feeds into one composited stream that\n  registers as a single UniFi camera. ffmpeg composites once via\n  filter_complex/xstack and publishes to go2rtc; UniFi and the preview\n  both pull the single stream.\n- Two-way audio: implement the ChangeTalkbackSettings handler to pump\n  Protect''s talkback audio through ffmpeg to a configurable per-camera\n  --talkback-url.\n\nIncludes unit tests for stream-source resolution, mosaic compose command,\nconfig-to-args wiring, and talkback schema.","tree":{"sha":"ac338eb1aa98fba75ff6791c498062b5cc228e50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/metril/unifi-camera-proxy/git/trees/ac338eb1aa98fba75ff6791c498062b5cc228e50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/metril/unifi-camera-proxy/git/commits/171f1850da0aa254e1e84b5a1f37552af163cb31","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"